  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, to the saints which are at Ephesus, and to the faithful in Christ Jesus:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Grace be to you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who hath blessed us with all spiritual blessings in heavenly places in Christ:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "According as he hath chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "To the praise of the glory of his grace, wherein he hath made us accepted in the beloved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "In whom we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the riches of his grace;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Wherein he hath abounded toward us in all wisdom and prudence;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Having made known unto us the mystery of his will, according to his good pleasure which he hath purposed in himself:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "That in the dispensation of the fulness of times he might gather together in one all things in Christ, both which are in heaven, and which are on earth; even in him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "In whom also we have obtained an inheritance, being predestinated according to the purpose of him who worketh all things after the counsel of his own will:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "That we should be to the praise of his glory, who first trusted in Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Which is the earnest of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Wherefore I also, after I heard of your faith in the Lord Jesus, and love unto all the saints,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Cease not to give thanks for you, making mention of you in my prayers;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give unto you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "The eyes of your understanding being enlightened; that ye may know what is the hope of his calling, and what the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "And what is the exceeding greatness of his power to us-ward who believe, according to the working of his mighty power,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Which he wrought in Christ, when he raised him from the dead, and set him at his own right hand in the heavenly places,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Far above all principality, and power, and might, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this world, but also in that which is to come:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "And hath put all things under his feet, and gave him to be the head over all things to the church,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:1:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Which is his body, the fulness of him that filleth all in all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 1:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:1:23"
      }
    }
  ],
